<p>The Vermin only teaze and pinch<br />
Their Foes superior by an Inch.<br />
So, Nat&#8217;ralists observe, a Flea<br />
Hath smaller Fleas that on him prey,<br />
And these have smaller yet to bite &#8217;em,<br />
And so proceed <em>ad infinitum</em>.</p>
<p>&#8212; Jonathan Swift</p>
<p>Great fleas have little fleas upon their backs to bite &#8217;em,<br />
And little fleas have lesser fleas, and so <em>ad infinitum</em>.<br />
And the great fleas themselves, in turn, have greater fleas to go on;<br />
While these again have greater still, and greater still, and so on.</p>
<p>&#8212; Augustus De Morgan</p>
